<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell July 6-8 Madras naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell July 6-8 Madras naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 27,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting from Madras July 6-8, a source close to IOC said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender offering the cargo from the east coast, closes June 25 and is valid until June 26.</p>
<p>IOC's last Madras LAN cargo, lifting in June, was awarded at $22 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis to a South Korean refiner, sources said.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
